  nibbles: ["I see a tall stranger. He's holding… (chew) …that part's gone now. Good luck, though.", "Sit, sit. Cut the cards. Don't cut them too small, I've only just had lunch.", "The Tower! A very bad— (chew) —mmph. Delicious. Forget about the Tower.", "The stars say… I ate the stars. They were on the card.", "Your future holds a great journey, or a great gravy. I've smudged it.", "I've been reading the cards for forty years. Eating them for forty-one.", "Beware of… hm. It's the corner. It's always the corner that's nicest.", "Your fortune's in your hand. Oh! May I? …That was your receipt.", "The Hanged Man means change. The Fool means you. They're both a bit chewy.", "You will meet someone. They'll be fine. I had most of the rest.", "Love's in your future, or lava. I'd stay flexible.", "I see water. I see fish. I see— (chew) —mm. Lot of salt in that one.", "Cards don't lie. They don't anything, once I'm done with them.", "That's the reading. If you want the other half, it'll be out by Thursday.", "Don't look at me like that. It's a very old and very digestive art."],
